<title>UK: Dorling Kindersley yr pretax profit up 37pct.</title>
<headline>Dorling Kindersley yr pretax profit up 37pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)(diluted)   15.2		   vs 11.6</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.0		    vs n/a</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 4.5		    vs 3.9</p>
<p> Pretax		     17.43		  vs 12.71</p>
<p> Turnover		   174.45		 vs 138.83</p>
<p> Operating result	 17.14		  vs 12.25</p>
<p> Interest		   0.29		   vs 0.46</p>
<p> Tax			  6.65		   vs 4.68</p>
<p> Net taxed		  10.78		  vs 8.03</p>
<p> Attributable	     10.78		  vs 8.02</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 4</p>
<p> Div registration date  November 5</p>
<p> Ex-div date		October 28</p>
<p>NOTE - Dorling Kindersley Holdings Plc produces illustrated reference books, CD-Roms and broadcast programmes.</p>
<p>Chairman Peter Kindersley said in a statement that the U.S. retail environment for multimedia &quot;is currently in a state of flux and more challenging than in the past.&quot;</p>
<p>He said the company believed a more stable market would emerge in due course.</p>
<p>Kindersley said the group's other businesses &quot;are also performing well,&quot; and that the company remained confident of the strength of its various businesses.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
